// Realms (D17, D642; docs/realm-two.md): what a world of a kind is, beyond its seed. A realm
// changes parts, materials and light, never the rules (docs/art-style.md). A kind with no row
// here is the first realm's: the land's own light and colours.
//   kind          the world's kind, as a save and a gate name it
//   name          what a player is told it is
//   beyond        the kind of the realm its gate leads to (D641)
//   plants_hue    how far its plants' own colours are turned round the hue circle, radians
//   ground        its ground's layers, a stack among the materials; the first realm's if not given
//   animals       the kinds of creature that live in it, by name; every kind if not given
//   sun, sky      its light against the first realm's: the sun's colour and the sky's (the
//                 horizon, the zenith, the shade), multiplied in, linear, red green blue
//   ground_low, ground_high, ground_steep, grass_dry, grass_lush, sand
//                 the land's colours, sRGB red green blue; left out, the land's own
//   ground_cover  how much of the grass and sand the ground could have is shown, 0 to 1
//   plants        the share of the first realm's trees and undergrowth that grow, 0 to 1
//   parts         what stands on its land by rule, each a catalogue item's model file
//                 (data/builds.ron) and how many of it a square kilometre holds
[
    (kind: "world", name: "the first realm", beyond: "industrial"),
    (
        kind: "industrial",
        name: "the industrial realm",
        beyond: "world",
        // A hazed amber day: the sun dulled and warmed, the sky greyed toward ochre.
        sun: Some((1.0, 0.8, 0.6)),
        sky: Some((0.82, 0.78, 0.74)),
        // Hardpan, stained gravel and slag: greys and rust, little that grows.
        ground_low: Some((0.36, 0.34, 0.32)),
        ground_high: Some((0.3, 0.29, 0.28)),
        ground_steep: Some((0.24, 0.22, 0.21)),
        grass_dry: Some((0.42, 0.36, 0.27)),
        grass_lush: Some((0.33, 0.34, 0.26)),
        sand: Some((0.45, 0.36, 0.3)),
        ground_cover: Some(0.25),
        // Its ground's own layers: gravel where the first realm has grass, asphalt and
        // cracked concrete where it has leaf litter (assets/materials/ground_industrial).
        ground: Some("ground_industrial"),
        // What does grow is parched: its greens turned toward ochre.
        plants_hue: Some(-0.4),
        // Little lives on a worked-out land: scavengers, and nothing in its den yet. A
        // stand-in until the realm has creatures of its own (D642: the developers').
        animals: Some(["Red fox", "Brown hare"]),
        // A worked-out land: one tree in ten.
        plants: Some(0.1),
        parts: [
            (file: "IndustrialPylon", a_km2: 20.0),
            (file: "IndustrialVentStack", a_km2: 25.0),
            (file: "IndustrialTank", a_km2: 25.0),
            (file: "IndustrialGenerator", a_km2: 30.0),
            (file: "IndustrialSign", a_km2: 20.0),
        ],
    ),
]
